97's model reproduced: 6 regions, 5 arms, 2 coordinates (ns per record, bits per element)
L0 = 5^6 = 15625

dominance, the claim in 97 section 10
  bitpack-carrier-d16            dominated at 0 of 6 regions
  bitpack-carrier-d32            dominated at 4 of 6 regions
  bitpack-carrier-d64            dominated at 6 of 6 regions
  bitpack-carrier-packed         dominated at 6 of 6 regions
  bitpack-carrier-packed-simd    dominated at 0 of 6 regions
  dominated in EVERY region: ['bitpack-carrier-d64', 'bitpack-carrier-packed']
  (97 section 10 names exactly these two)

counts on 97's model
  L0 any section                      15625
  L1 Pareto-admissible                  144
  L3 rationalisable, w >= 0              72   <- 97 section 2.2 reports 72 here
  L4 rationalisable, w > 0                9
  L5 forced, w > 0                        9   <- 97 section 2.2 reports 9 strict

the two sentences, measured against each other
  sections at L3 that select an arm 97 says no weighting can select: 63 of 72
  sections at L4 that do:                                            0 of 9

  So both sentences are true and they are about different rungs. The
  headline count admits a zero weight, and a zero weight is exactly
  what lets a strategy pick a dominated arm. The dominance claim is
  about strictly positive weights, where it holds by construction.

  the sections that survive at L4, listed, since there are few
