    ['d16', 'd16', 'd16', 'packed-simd', 'd16', 'd16']
    ['d16', 'd16', 'd16', 'packed-simd', 'packed-simd', 'd16']
    ['d16', 'd16', 'packed-simd', 'packed-simd', 'packed-simd', 'd16']
    ['d16', 'd16', 'packed-simd', 'packed-simd', 'packed-simd', 'packed-simd']
    ['d32', 'd16', 'd16', 'd16', 'd16', 'd16']
    ['d32', 'd32', 'd16', 'd16', 'd16', 'd16']
    ['packed-simd', 'd16', 'packed-simd', 'packed-simd', 'packed-simd', 'packed-simd']
    ['packed-simd', 'packed-simd', 'packed-simd', 'packed-simd', 'packed-simd', 'packed-simd']

what to carry, and what not
  Not '72 of 15625'. That figure counts sections a strategy could
  only reach by ignoring a measurement outright.
  The figure with the property 97 wants from it is 9 of 15625, which is 0.0576%, and it is
  smaller than the one reported, so 97's conclusion that a weighting
  admits a vanishing fraction of the sections is strengthened rather
  than weakened by the correction.

